# Pull requests start from current main

Every commit that goes into a pull request is based on the latest `origin/main`. Fetch it immediately before creating the branch or committing.

```sh
git fetch origin main
git checkout -b feat/example origin/main
```

- The pull request base is `main`.
- If `origin/main` moved after the branch was created, rebase onto the fetched tip and update the remote branch with `git push --force-with-lease` before opening or updating the pull request.
- Drop commits that are already on `origin/main`.
- Do not force-push `main`.

```
# ❌ BAD
git checkout feat/other-work
git checkout -b feat/new-thing
# parent is another feature branch, or a local main that was not just fetched

# ✅ GOOD
git fetch origin main
git checkout -b feat/new-thing origin/main
```
